From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: codecs: add the MediaTek MT6368 capture path

The analog inputs, preamplifiers, ADCs and the link to the AFE of the MT6368,
from the MediaTek driver in the OnePlus kernel
(oneplus/mt6897_b_16.0.0_oneplus_pad) and the Lenovo one, in the shape of
mt6359.c. The earpiece, the line and headphone outputs, voice wakeup and the
digital microphones are left for when something needs them.

The ADC and preamplifier selectors stay disconnected until the card sets them.
The calibration of the link's phases runs in the machine driver, on the data
pins that loop the test pulse back.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/Kconfig  |   7 +
 sound/soc/codecs/Makefile |   2 +
 sound/soc/codecs/mt6368.c | 991 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 sound/soc/codecs/mt6368.h | 203 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 1203 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/codecs/mt6368.c
 create mode 100644 sound/soc/codecs/mt6368.h

